The Saionji family was a court noble who descended from the Fujiwara clan.
He was from the Kanin line of the Northern House of the Fujiwara clan, and his family rank was Seiga family (the Seiga family).
The Toin family and the Imadegawa family (the Kikutei family) were divided into the Saionji family.
In addition, the Saionji clan in Iyo Province was a powerful branch of the Saionji clan who used the name of Saionji.
The family crest is the left Mitsudomoe.
The Saionji family was founded by FUJIWARA no Michisue, the third son of FUJIWARA no Kinzane.
When Michisue's great-grandson, Kintsune SAIONJI, had been a niece of MINAMOTO no Yoritomo, he was confined to the Imperial Court as a relative of the Kamakura bakufu (Japanese feudal government headed by a shogun) during the Jokyu War, and after the disturbance, he was trusted by the bakufu and became the head of the Imperial Court as Kanto moshitsugi (an official in charge of controlling the Kanto region) and raised the family status as Daijo daijin (Grand minister of state).
The family name of Saien-ji Temple is derived from the name of a temple built by Kintsune in a villa in Kyoto (Kitayama-so, Kadono-gun, Yamashiro Province).
This hall was also called Kitayama-dono, and the current Kinkaku-ji Temple was transferred from the Saionji family to the temple.
After Kintsune, he received support from the Kamakura bakufu (Japanese feudal government headed by a shogun) and had power over the Sekke (line of regents and advisers) throughout the Kamakura period.
Sanekane SAIONJI approached Daikakuji-to (imperial lineage starting with Emperor Kameyama) and had a daughter of Emperor Kameyama and Emperor Godaigo.
However, after his son, Kinhira SAIONJI, the Daikakuji-to (imperial lineage starting with Emperor Kameyama), he supported the Daikakuji-to (imperial lineage starting with Emperor Kameyama) and deepened confrontation with Daikakuji-to (imperial lineage starting with Emperor Kameyama).
After that, the Kamakura bakufu (Japanese feudal government headed by a shogun) was overthrown at the time of Kinmune SAIONJI, and was dismissed from the post of Kanto moshitsugi.
Kinmune sheltered Yasuie HOJO (Tokiokioki) who was the remnants of the Hojo clan, and assassinated Emperor Godaigo, who started the Kenmu Restoration, and plotted to support the Retired Emperor GofDaigo in the Jimyoin line, and Kinmune was arrested by his younger brother Kinshige SAIONJI.
During the period of the Northern and Southern Courts, Sanetoshi SAIONJI, the son of Kinmune, served the Northern Court (Japan) and rose to Udaijin (Minister of the Right) and restored his family name.
During the Muromachi period and the Edo period, it was also known as a family business of biwa (Japanese lute).
