It is said that Yoshihisa TOKUGAWA, who succeeded Yoshinobu, was also called 'Keikyu-yo' along with Yoshinobu.
There are two names of 'keiki-yo' and 'keiki-san,' and it is considered that the term of 'keiki-san' is rare even today, but it is often confirmed not only in Shizuoka but also in the case of 'keiki-san.'
