Amenooshihomimi, who was suppressed by Ashihara no Nakatsukuni (the Central Land of Reed Plains) and descended to earth, was born while Ninigi was born.
Contemplation
In the mythology, there is a view that Amaterasu Omikami (the Sun Goddess) is an incarnation of the gods (Takamimusubi) who was born earlier than him, because there is a scene in which Amaterasu Omikami (the Sun Goddess) was ordered to perform religious services.
There is also a view that the shrine became a deity of ancient miko (shrine maidens).
The other name 'Hirume' refers to a miko who served the sun god.
The sun god was originally a male god, but there is a theory that the miko who served it was the same as the sun god and became a female god.
Also, there is a theory that this god was established during the reign of the Empress Jito, and it is said that Himiko was the model of Amaterasu Omikami (the Sun Goddess).
It is pointed out that the birth of the moon from the sun of Amaterasu Omikami (the Sun Goddess) and the moon of Tsukuyomi (the sun god of the moon) is 'the moon' in "Ryoho Gofujo" (previously written in the sixth century) (the first half of the sixth century), and 'the eyes of the left eye on the eyes of the moon' is the 'the moon' and 'the eyes of the left eye of the moon' is the same as the moon, and the moon is strongly influenced by the Taoism of the moon.
