In comparison, it is pointed out that the birth of Amaterasu Omikami (the Sun Goddess) is similar to that of the old times (the third century) that records the birth of the myth of Amaterasu Omikami (the Sun Goddess).
There is also a theory that it is a myth that it was introduced to Japan along with the transition of ethnic groups during the preceding period, because it is popular in Asia.
